Privacy Policy

Last updated: September 14, 2026

National Dominance ("the App") is made by twelve52 LLC ("we", "us", "our"). This page explains what information the App handles and what you can do about it.

Playing without an account
Your game saves, settings, and progress are stored on your device. You can play the whole game this way. We never see that data, and it stays on your device until you delete the App.

Playing with an account
Competing on the daily ladders, raiding other players, and joining a bloc are optional and require signing in with Apple. When you sign in, we create an account for you on our servers. It holds:

The ID Apple assigns to you, and an email address if Apple shares one with us (Apple can give you a private relay address instead of your real one)
Your display name, and the nation and region you chose
Your Game Center player ID, which we use to keep one person from running several accounts
Your daily scores, ladder standing, raid history, and bloc membership
A push notification token, only if you allow notifications about raids

Your display name, nation, and scores are visible to other players on the boards, and your nation can be raided by other players. We use this data only to run the competition. We do not sell it, and we do not share it with advertisers.

Deleting your account
You can delete your account at any time inside the App. Go to Settings, then Account, then Delete Account. Everything listed above is removed from our servers right away. Your local saves stay on your device. If you ever have trouble with this, email us and we will remove it for you.

Advertising
Ads are provided by Google AdMob. Google may use your device's advertising identifier, IP address, and usage data to show and measure ads. Google's privacy policy is at policies.google.com/privacy. When the App first asks, you decide whether to allow tracking across other apps and websites. You can change that later under Settings, Privacy, Tracking on your device. Where the law requires it, an Ad Privacy Options button appears in the App's Settings. You can also remove ads with a one-time purchase.

Purchases
All purchases go through Apple. We never receive or store your payment details.

Game Center
If you use Game Center, Apple handles your Game Center profile and leaderboard data under Apple's privacy policy at apple.com/privacy.

Notifications
Reminders and raid alerts are optional. You can turn them off in the App's Settings or on your device at any time.

Children
The App is not directed at children under 13, and we do not knowingly collect personal information from them.

Changes
If this policy changes, the new version will appear on this page with an updated date.

Contact
Questions about this policy: general@twelve52cards.com
